      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-constant-electric-orbit",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Exact relativistic orbit in a uniform electric field",
        "statement": "In the flat Minkowski specialization of [[def-rpm-charge-spin-model]], adopt the fixed-endpoint external-charge action [[post-rpm-external-charge-action]], its conditional stationary-action equivalence [[pthm-rpm-external-charge-action-equivalence]], the flat massive-particle momentum model [[post-sr-massive-particle-dynamics]], and $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ of [[def-countable-choice]] for the canonical tangent-bundle smooth structure required by the current local IVP and action-equivalence carriers. Let $m>0$ in kilograms, $q\\in\\mathbb R$ in coulombs, $c>0$ in metres per second, and $E_0\\in\\mathbb R$ in newtons per coulomb; let the uniform field in one named inertial SI chart be $\\mathbf E=E_0e_1$, $\\mathbf B=0$. A smooth global potential is $\\phi=-E_0x^1$, $\\mathbf A=0$, so the local-potential hypothesis is satisfied. Spatial coordinates are in metres, coordinate time $t$ is in seconds, and initial momenta are in kilograms metres per second. Set $F_0=qE_0$ (newtons), take initial event $(0,\\mathbf x_0)$ and initial momentum $\\mathbf p_0=(p_{01},\\mathbf p_\\perp)$ at $t=0$, and define $\\Pi$ (momentum units), $\\mathcal E$ (joules) and $\\mathbf v$ (metres per second) by\n\n$$p_1(t)=p_{01}+F_0t,\\qquad \\Pi=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+|\\mathbf p_\\perp|^2}>0,\\qquad \\mathcal E(t)=c\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_1(t)^2},\\qquad \\mathbf v(t)=\\frac{c(p_1(t)e_1+\\mathbf p_\\perp)}{\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_1(t)^2}}.$$\n\nIf $F_0\\ne0$, the exact position for every $t\\in\\mathbb R$ is\n\n$$x^1(t)=x^1_0+\\frac c{F_0}\\left(\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_1(t)^2}-\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_{01}^2}\\right),$$\n$$\\mathbf x_\\perp(t)=\\mathbf x_{\\perp0}+\\frac{c\\mathbf p_\\perp}{F_0}\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{p_1(t)+\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_1(t)^2}}{p_{01}+\\sqrt{\\Pi^2+p_{01}^2}}\\right).$$\n\nIf $F_0=0$, the field exerts no force on the particle and the orbit is free:\n$\\mathbf p(t)=\\mathbf p_0$, $\\mathcal E(t)=\\mathcal E(0)$ and\n$\\mathbf x(t)=\\mathbf x_0+c^2\\mathbf p_0t/\\mathcal E(0)$. These formulas define future-timelike worldlines for all finite coordinate times; any model solution with the same data agrees with them on every common connected time interval. This is a conditional model deduction, not evidence that the adopted action describes a measured particle.",
        "deps": [
          "def-rpm-charge-spin-model",
          "post-rpm-external-charge-action",
