      {
        "id": "pthm-rpm-crossed-field-drift",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Subcritical crossed fields and exact drift-frame orbits",
        "statement": "In the flat SI charged-particle model with adopted action, conditional force equation, flat massive-particle momentum model, and $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ assumption required by the current local RPM carriers [[post-rpm-external-charge-action]], [[pthm-rpm-external-charge-action-equivalence]], [[pthm-rpm-charge-mass-shell]], [[post-sr-massive-particle-dynamics]], and [[def-countable-choice]], let $m>0$ be in kilograms, $q$ in coulombs, $c$ in metres per second, $E_0$ in newtons per coulomb, and $B_0$ in tesla. Use an inertial chart with $x^0=ct$ and all coordinates in metres, so $t$ is in seconds. Set $\\mathbf E=E_0e_1$, $\\mathbf B=B_0e_3$, $B_0\\ne0$, and $|E_0|<c|B_0|$. Use the smooth combined potential $\\phi=-E_0x^1$, $\\mathbf A=(-B_0x^2/2,B_0x^1/2,0)$. Define\n\n$$\\mathbf v_d=\\frac{\\mathbf E\\times\\mathbf B}{|\\mathbf B|^2}=-\\frac{E_0}{B_0}e_2,\\qquad \\gamma_d=(1-|\\mathbf v_d|^2/c^2)^{-1/2}.$$\n\nThe drift velocity has units of metres per second and $\\gamma_d$ is dimensionless.\n\nThe passive Lorentz boost of velocity $\\mathbf v_d$ transforms these fields to $\\mathbf E'=0$, $\\mathbf B'=\\mathbf B/\\gamma_d$. Consequently every flat-model solution in the laboratory frame is the inverse boost of the uniform-magnetic-field orbit of [[pthm-rpm-constant-magnetic-helix]] with the boosted initial data. The laboratory coordinate time increases strictly and ranges over all real values along that inverse-boosted orbit. In particular, the constant velocity $\\mathbf v=\\mathbf v_d$ is an exact solution because $\\mathbf E+\\mathbf v_d\\times\\mathbf B=0$. Other initial data give boosted helical orbits; the theorem does not identify every velocity with $\\mathbf v_d$. The cases $|E_0|=c|B_0|$ and $|E_0|>c|B_0|$ are outside the statement.",
