        "title": "Two stationary clocks and one radial Rindler ray",
        "statement": "Specialize [[pthm-rpm-rindler-clock-gradient]] to $a=2\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}}$, emission radius $\\rho_E=2\\,\\mathrm m$, reception radius $\\rho_R=4\\,\\mathrm m$, and a future outward radial ray. These are exact model parameters. The one-way coordinate travel time is $(c/2\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-2}})\\log 2$, and over a shared Rindler-time interval the ideal-clock ratio is $\\Delta\\tau_R/\\Delta\\tau_E=2$. The instantaneous received-frequency ratio is $\\omega_R/\\omega_E=1/2$ under the theorem's additional adopted local phase-reception rule, with its local ray-regime and short-observation qualifications for finite apparatus and no numerical error bound or empirical validation. No experiment is described.",
