        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Uniform electric field from rest",
        "statement": "Choose $m=1\\,\\mathrm{kg}$, $q=1\\,\\mathrm C$, $E_0=2\\,\\mathrm{N\\,C^{-1}}$, $\\mathbf B=0$, and initial data $\\mathbf x_0=0\\,\\mathrm m$, $\\mathbf p_0=0\\,\\mathrm{kg\\,m\\,s^{-1}}$ at $t=0$ in [[pthm-rpm-constant-electric-orbit]]. Coordinate time $t$ is in seconds. Then $F_0=2\\,\\mathrm N$, $p_1(t)=F_0t$, and for every finite $t$ the model orbit is\n\n$$x^1(t)=\\frac c{F_0}\\left(\\sqrt{m^2c^2+F_0^2t^2}-mc\\right),\\qquad x^2(t)=x^3(t)=0,$$\n\nwith $v_1(t)=cF_0t/\\sqrt{m^2c^2+F_0^2t^2}$. This is a symbolic model calculation with chosen parameters, not a report of measured field or particle data.",
