        "id": "ex-rpm-constant-magnetic-helix",
        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "A circular magnetic orbit with zero axial momentum",
        "statement": "In [[pthm-rpm-constant-magnetic-helix]], choose $qB_0>0$, $p_{01}=p_*>0$ with units kilogram metre per second, $p_{02}=p_{03}=0$, and arbitrary $m>0$ kilograms. Then $S_0=\\sqrt{m^2c^2+p_*^2}$ has momentum units, $\\gamma_0=S_0/(mc)$ is dimensionless and $\\Omega=qB_0/(\\gamma_0m)>0$ has units inverse seconds. The orbit is the circle\n\n$$x^1=x^1_0+\\frac{cp_*}{S_0\\Omega}\\sin(\\Omega t),\\qquad x^2=x^2_0-\\frac{cp_*}{S_0\\Omega}\\bigl(1-\\cos(\\Omega t)\\bigr),\\qquad x^3=x^3_0,$$\n\nof radius $p_*/(qB_0)$, with constant energy $cS_0$. At $t=\\pi/(2\\Omega)$ its momentum is $(0,-p_*,0)$. All values are model parameters, not observations.",
