        "kind": "example",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "The exact constant drift solution in subcritical crossed fields",
        "statement": "Let $B_0>0$ be in tesla and set $E_0=cB_0/2$ in newtons per coulomb, so $\\mathbf E=E_0e_1$, $\\mathbf B=B_0e_3$ is subcritical. In [[pthm-rpm-crossed-field-drift]], the drift velocity and boost factor are $\\mathbf v_d=-(c/2)e_2$ in metres per second and $\\gamma_d=2/\\sqrt3$. The constant-velocity orbit $\\mathbf x(t)=\\mathbf x_0+\\mathbf v_dt$ in a chart with $x^0=ct$ solves the adopted model for any $m>0$ and constant charge $q$: its Lorentz force vanishes. This is one exact solution; other initial data yield boosted magnetic orbits.",
